WEBVTT

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:17.850
"Hiyori Minagi"        "Osamu Mukai"
"Risa Fuchihara"        "Koharu Minagi"

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:20.970
Why though?

00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:27.230
Well, we're sisters, so I figured
we'd be in different classes.

00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:28.860
Hiyori...

00:00:30.070 --> 00:00:33.280
How are you so calm?

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:38.530
We're literally being torn apart!

00:00:38.530 --> 00:00:41.040
Wow, you're a handful, aren't you?

00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:46.790
I'm so nervous.

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:55.630
Koi!

00:00:55.630 --> 00:00:57.840
Morning, Yamahi.

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:01.510
I'm so glad we're in the same class.

00:01:01.510 --> 00:01:05.100
I see that you're still shy even
though we're in high school now.

00:01:06.350 --> 00:01:09.860
But it looks like things will go well
with your new older sister.

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:13.190
I hear she's very sociable.

00:01:13.190 --> 00:01:17.610
Yeah, you could say that. And she
seems to be interested in fishing, too.

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:18.990
But...

00:01:20.120 --> 00:01:22.450
In that case, Yamahi...

00:02:54.250 --> 00:02:58.050
"Episode 2"
"If You Can Just Smile"

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:01.930
How was your new class?

00:03:01.930 --> 00:03:06.180
Huh? It took everything I had
just to remember my teacher's face.

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:09.520
I managed to get the
contact info of a few people.

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:12.400
Though I didn't really
remember their faces.

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:13.650
How does that work?

00:03:13.650 --> 00:03:16.690
It's all about enthusiasm.

00:03:16.690 --> 00:03:19.400
Oh, Koharu. This way.

00:03:20.740 --> 00:03:25.080
There's somewhere I'd like to go with you.

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:27.660
Is that okay?

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:30.080
Sure!

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:35.670
This is a fly-fishing specialty shop
that's run by my childhood friend's dad.

00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:37.130
Your childhood friend?

00:03:37.130 --> 00:03:40.470
Yup. I've been friends
with her since nursery school.

00:03:40.470 --> 00:03:42.220
Wow, so you actually have friends!

00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:45.430
Could you not say something so rude
with a huge smile on your face?!

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:48.310
Hello.

00:03:48.310 --> 00:03:50.020
Hey.

00:03:53.350 --> 00:03:55.650
There's so much stuff!

00:03:57.480 --> 00:03:59.730
Koi, I brought Koharu with me.

00:03:59.730 --> 00:04:02.820
I'm her big sister Koharu!

00:04:02.820 --> 00:04:05.030
I've heard quite a bit about you.

00:04:05.030 --> 00:04:06.660
This is Koi Yoshinaga.

00:04:06.660 --> 00:04:08.790
She's in Class 1 with me.

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:10.540
Pleasure.

00:04:10.540 --> 00:04:13.620
Koi! What a cute name!

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:17.590
Since your family runs a fishing shop,
were you named after the fish?

00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:24.090
Of course not. My name means "love."

00:04:24.090 --> 00:04:25.590
Oh, I see.

00:04:25.590 --> 00:04:30.770
K-Koharu. You see, I always shop here.

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:34.230
Other than general fishing goods,
they also have materials.

00:04:34.230 --> 00:04:36.020
It's a lot of fun to look at.

00:04:36.020 --> 00:04:37.480
Materials?

00:04:37.480 --> 00:04:41.230
Materials for fly fishing.
Like fishing threads and stuff.

00:04:41.230 --> 00:04:43.530
It's like an arts and crafts store!

00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:45.410
We have stuff like this, too.

00:04:45.410 --> 00:04:46.780
A bird?!

00:04:46.780 --> 00:04:47.240
"The Fishes' Counterattack"

00:04:46.780 --> 00:04:47.240
A bird?!

00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:49.450
"The Fishes' Counterattack"

00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:49.450
You fish with bird corpses?!

00:04:49.450 --> 00:04:51.540
"The Fishes' Counterattack"

00:04:49.450 --> 00:04:51.540
We use their feathers!

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:52.040
We use their feathers!

00:04:52.040 --> 00:04:55.460
And here's a fly wrapped in said feathers.

00:04:55.460 --> 00:04:58.710
This looks different
from the one Hiyori has.

00:04:58.710 --> 00:05:02.090
You can basically split up flies
in four categories.

00:05:02.090 --> 00:05:02.170
Dry, wet, nymph, and streamer.

00:05:02.170 --> 00:05:02.920
"Dry"

00:05:02.170 --> 00:05:02.920
Dry, wet, nymph, and streamer.

00:05:02.920 --> 00:05:03.670
"Wet"
"Dry"
Dry, wet, nymph, and streamer.

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:04.420
"Nymph"
"Wet"
"Dry"

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:04.420
Dry, wet, nymph, and streamer.

00:05:04.420 --> 00:05:06.260
"Nymph"
"Wet"
"Streamer"

00:05:04.420 --> 00:05:06.260
Dry, wet, nymph, and streamer.

00:05:06.260 --> 00:05:06.510
Dry, wet, nymph, and streamer.

00:05:06.510 --> 00:05:08.510
This one here is a dry one.

00:05:08.510 --> 00:05:10.510
I'm getting bombarded with all
these non-Japanese words again...

00:05:10.510 --> 00:05:14.430
I'm sorry, ma'am.
She's allergic to foreign words.

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:15.890
"Koharu"

00:05:15.890 --> 00:05:18.360
"Koharu"
You float dry flies on top of the water.

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:21.020
"Koharu"
It's supposed to look like a
bug floating on top of the water.

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:23.650
"Koharu"
So fishies eat bugs, huh?

00:05:23.650 --> 00:05:26.700
Nymphs are flies you sink
to the bottom of the ocean.

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:29.990
A lot of them look like
the larvae of aquatic bugs.

00:05:29.990 --> 00:05:33.870
Those poor things. Getting gobbled
up while they're still kids.

00:05:33.870 --> 00:05:37.170
Wet flies are somewhere
in between dry and nymphs.

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:40.920
You make them look like molting bugs or
bugs being carried away by the water.

00:05:40.920 --> 00:05:43.460
So they're like going through puberty?

00:05:43.460 --> 00:05:46.510
Streamers are flies that are
supposed to look like little fish.

00:05:46.510 --> 00:05:49.140
You mostly use those in
lakes and in the ocean.

00:05:49.140 --> 00:05:52.390
Oh, that's the one you were using, Hiyori.

00:05:52.390 --> 00:05:57.940
And you can find all four kinds in
my greedy little artificial fly set.

00:05:57.940 --> 00:06:00.690
Congratulations, Yamahi, on being
the proud new owner of this set.

00:06:00.690 --> 00:06:04.360
Oh, right. I ordered this the other day.

00:06:04.360 --> 00:06:09.320
Yamahi and her dad were both regulars.
Thanks for keeping us in business.

00:06:09.320 --> 00:06:11.160
Oh, I see.

00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:15.160
Since your family runs a fishing shop,
does your dad fish, too, Koi?

00:06:16.290 --> 00:06:17.910
K-Koharu!

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:22.630
That's putting it lightly.

00:06:22.630 --> 00:06:25.710
You call monsters
like him fishing addicts.

00:06:25.710 --> 00:06:27.340
Eek...

00:06:27.340 --> 00:06:32.100
Fishing, fishing, fishing, fishing always
takes priority. He's absolutely demented!

00:06:32.100 --> 00:06:35.520
Yeah, that's right. As soon
as I got home from school,

00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:38.180
he left all the work to me
and ran off to fish again.

00:06:38.180 --> 00:06:39.770
She's on a roll now.

00:06:39.770 --> 00:06:42.110
That's pretty rotten for
a parent to do right after

00:06:42.110 --> 00:06:43.770
his daughter got into high school, right?

00:06:43.770 --> 00:06:45.280
Oh, that's just the beginning though.

00:06:45.280 --> 00:06:48.240
Even when I was born...

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:51.910
Mr. Yoshinaga, your wife's on the phone.
Her contractions have started!

00:06:51.910 --> 00:06:56.830
But they're totally rising right now!
I'm definitely gonna catch one!

00:06:56.830 --> 00:06:59.750
Uh, dude...

00:06:59.750 --> 00:07:01.370
From what I heard,

00:07:01.370 --> 00:07:05.880
apparently my father finally showed up to
the hospital five hours after I was born.

00:07:07.380 --> 00:07:10.510
He happened to catch
a giant koi fish then,

00:07:10.510 --> 00:07:13.970
so he tried to name me after the fish.

00:07:13.970 --> 00:07:17.310
But my mom tried to stop him
and at least changed the kanji.

00:07:17.310 --> 00:07:20.140
She really was named after the fish...

00:07:20.140 --> 00:07:23.150
The worst part about all of this...

00:07:23.150 --> 00:07:27.070
Is the fact that he's actually
proud of his perversion!

00:07:27.070 --> 00:07:27.280
"Sorry not sorry"

00:07:27.070 --> 00:07:27.280
Is the fact that he's actually
proud of his perversion!

00:07:27.280 --> 00:07:29.530
"Sorry not sorry"

00:07:27.280 --> 00:07:29.530
You can just call me a hermit.

00:07:29.530 --> 00:07:31.240
"Sorry not sorry"

00:07:29.530 --> 00:07:31.240
Wow.

00:07:31.240 --> 00:07:31.450
Wow.

00:07:31.450 --> 00:07:34.490
Was your dad some weirdo, too, Hiyori?

00:07:34.490 --> 00:07:36.450
I can't even deny that.

00:07:36.450 --> 00:07:39.870
No, no. Papa Yamahi
actually had common sense.

00:07:39.870 --> 00:07:41.330
You think so?

00:07:41.330 --> 00:07:46.000
Well, my dad was lamenting about how
your dad wouldn't go fishing with him

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:47.920
until you finished grade school.

00:07:47.920 --> 00:07:51.800
He was a great dad
that always put his family first.

00:07:53.470 --> 00:07:57.850
Hey, is this "Yamahi" person
you keep talking about Hiyori?

00:07:57.850 --> 00:08:00.850
Yup. That's the nickname I gave her.

00:08:00.850 --> 00:08:01.230
"Aoi Yamakawa"
"Hiyori Yamakawa"

00:08:00.850 --> 00:08:01.230
Yup. That's the nickname I gave her.

00:08:01.230 --> 00:08:05.110
"Aoi Yamakawa"
"Hiyori Yamakawa"

00:08:01.230 --> 00:08:05.110
When we were in grade school,
there were two Yamakawas in our class.

00:08:05.110 --> 00:08:08.820
"Aoi Yamakawa"
"Hiyori Yamakawa"

00:08:05.110 --> 00:08:08.820
So I decided to shorten Hiyori Yamakawa
and started calling her Yamahi.

00:08:08.820 --> 00:08:09.070
So I decided to shorten Hiyori Yamakawa
and started calling her Yamahi.

00:08:09.070 --> 00:08:12.950
Though it never really caught on and you
were the only one who ever called me that.

00:08:12.950 --> 00:08:14.820
How nostalgic.

00:08:14.820 --> 00:08:18.410
Oh, I heard that Kimuracchi
went to an all girls' school.

00:08:18.410 --> 00:08:19.870
The one where all the rich girls go to.

00:08:19.870 --> 00:08:24.870
Oh, really? She was pretty lively,
so I'm a bit surprised.

00:08:27.130 --> 00:08:29.170
Is something wrong, Koharu?

00:08:29.170 --> 00:08:30.550
No.

00:08:30.550 --> 00:08:33.260
Even if you were talking about
the past I wouldn't know about

00:08:33.260 --> 00:08:35.180
or even if she was calling you
a special nickname,

00:08:35.180 --> 00:08:38.100
I'm not jealous at all, okay?

00:08:38.100 --> 00:08:40.020
She's an open book.

00:08:40.020 --> 00:08:43.520
And you're not Yamahi anymore.
Since your last name is Minagi now

00:08:43.520 --> 00:08:45.270
you'd be Minahi!

00:08:45.270 --> 00:08:47.360
Minahi...

00:08:47.360 --> 00:08:52.070
Oh, hey. There's one other place
I'd like to go to. Is that okay?

00:08:52.070 --> 00:08:55.280
What? Are you going to
take me to see your boyfriend

00:08:55.280 --> 00:08:57.820
now that we've met your childhood friend?

00:08:57.820 --> 00:09:00.160
I don't have a boyfriend!

00:09:02.620 --> 00:09:05.500
The place we're about to go to...

00:09:05.500 --> 00:09:10.300
...is the place my dad took me to
all the time when I was little.

00:09:12.090 --> 00:09:15.720
I love that the ocean is
literally in walking distance!

00:09:15.720 --> 00:09:16.970
R-Really?

00:09:16.970 --> 00:09:21.260
I mean, we can swim all we want
in the summer! That's so cool!

00:09:21.260 --> 00:09:25.190
I really don't like crowds, so I don't
come here in the summer often.

00:09:25.190 --> 00:09:29.360
I can't believe we raised you to be so
spoiled! You disappoint me, Little Sister!

00:09:29.360 --> 00:09:31.980
I definitely don't
remember you raising me.

00:09:34.530 --> 00:09:37.570
Are we... going up this thing?

00:09:37.570 --> 00:09:39.490
Are you afraid of heights?

00:09:39.490 --> 00:09:42.870
Nope! I'm totally fine!
Let's do this! Yeah!

00:09:42.870 --> 00:09:45.500
You're so easy to read...

00:09:50.500 --> 00:09:54.090
Was the ceiling always this low?

00:09:54.090 --> 00:09:56.720
The staircase seems narrower, too.

00:09:56.720 --> 00:09:59.640
When I was smaller...

00:09:59.640 --> 00:10:04.310
I'm scared... I don't wanna, Daddy.

00:10:05.480 --> 00:10:07.810
Come here, Hiyori.

00:10:07.810 --> 00:10:12.190
Daddy will be right here.
It's not scary at all.

00:10:14.070 --> 00:10:15.740
Okay.

00:10:20.780 --> 00:10:23.540
We're pretty high up, Hiyori.

00:10:23.540 --> 00:10:27.410
Is that handrail going to hold up?
It won't break, will it?

00:10:28.790 --> 00:10:30.710
It'll be fine.

00:10:32.250 --> 00:10:33.840
Okay.

00:10:41.760 --> 00:10:43.760
It's so pretty.

00:10:50.690 --> 00:10:53.900
Koharu, here.

00:10:53.900 --> 00:10:55.440
It's for you.

00:10:55.440 --> 00:10:58.740
The greedy little fly set
you bought earlier...

00:10:58.740 --> 00:11:00.410
You're giving it to me?

00:11:00.410 --> 00:11:02.070
Yup.

00:11:03.580 --> 00:11:06.660
Let's go fishing Sunday
at a supervised spot.

00:11:06.660 --> 00:11:07.910
Supervised?

00:11:07.910 --> 00:11:09.790
A designated spot for fishing.

00:11:09.790 --> 00:11:11.330
Koi said going to a designated spot first

00:11:11.330 --> 00:11:15.250
might be good if you
want to learn fly fishing.

00:11:15.250 --> 00:11:19.510
Koi said she'd ask her dad
to give us a ride.

00:11:19.510 --> 00:11:21.510
Koi's super nice!

00:11:21.510 --> 00:11:24.680
You can use my dad's
fishing rod that's back at home.

00:11:24.680 --> 00:11:26.010
I'm sure you'll catch something.

00:11:26.010 --> 00:11:28.600
Ooh, I'm super excited!

00:11:29.850 --> 00:11:31.310
So, hey...

00:11:32.810 --> 00:11:36.360
Thanks for hanging out with me today.

00:11:36.360 --> 00:11:42.110
To the shop I usually go to
and my favorite spot... Um...

00:11:42.110 --> 00:11:44.780
I really wanted you to see them.

00:11:49.620 --> 00:11:52.620
Thank you so much for showing me.

00:11:55.210 --> 00:11:56.710
Well, we should probably head home.

00:11:56.710 --> 00:11:59.960
Yeah. What should we have for dinner?

00:11:59.960 --> 00:12:03.430
We definitely still have
plenty of fish in the fridge.

00:12:03.430 --> 00:12:05.720
Sorry about that...

00:12:06.850 --> 00:12:08.600
Koi!

00:12:08.600 --> 00:12:11.230
I came up totally empty today!

00:12:11.230 --> 00:12:12.190
Empty!

00:12:12.190 --> 00:12:13.140
Empty!

00:12:13.140 --> 00:12:14.310
--Empty! Empty!
--Just get the shrimps
into the bath already.

00:12:14.310 --> 00:12:16.860
--Empty!
--Empty! Empty!
--Just get the shrimps
into the bath already.

00:12:18.070 --> 00:12:19.650
Be careful, okay?

00:12:19.650 --> 00:12:20.940
We will.

00:12:20.940 --> 00:12:23.490
I had no idea you leave
so early for fishing.

00:12:23.490 --> 00:12:28.030
Morning and evenings are best for fishing,
so anglers start their days off early.

00:12:28.030 --> 00:12:29.200
I see...

00:12:29.200 --> 00:12:32.460
But it's not absolutely certain.

00:12:32.460 --> 00:12:35.710
There are times you can't catch
any because you're just so tired,

00:12:35.710 --> 00:12:37.880
and if you're fishing in the ocean,
you have to think about the tide--

00:12:37.880 --> 00:12:39.210
That's enough, Dad.

00:12:39.210 --> 00:12:41.050
Ow, ow, ow!

00:12:41.050 --> 00:12:44.220
Okay, we're going to catch
a bunch of stuff for dinner!

00:12:44.220 --> 00:12:45.890
Have a wonderful time.

00:12:45.890 --> 00:12:48.300
See you later!

00:13:02.990 --> 00:13:05.110
And we're here.

00:13:11.040 --> 00:13:13.960
This place is huge!

00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:18.250
I thought it'd be a
much smaller fishing hole,

00:13:18.250 --> 00:13:20.130
so I'm super excited right now!

00:13:20.130 --> 00:13:21.800
Good for you...

00:13:28.890 --> 00:13:31.220
Are you in celebrity mode now, Koi?

00:13:31.220 --> 00:13:33.480
I'm avoiding the sun.

00:13:33.480 --> 00:13:37.980
I'll go get us registered, but this
is your first time, right, Koharu?

00:13:37.980 --> 00:13:40.270
Want me to set up your rod for you?

00:13:40.270 --> 00:13:41.860
It's okay!

00:13:44.280 --> 00:13:45.780
"Bam"

00:13:45.820 --> 00:13:47.030
"Bam"

00:13:47.070 --> 00:13:49.990
"Babam"

00:13:49.990 --> 00:13:52.910
"Babam"
That's great,
but let's attach the fly now.

00:13:52.910 --> 00:13:54.120
"Babam"

00:13:54.750 --> 00:13:58.250
The greedy little fly set
is making its debut!

00:13:58.250 --> 00:14:01.590
First, you're going to go
through the hole at the top,

00:14:01.590 --> 00:14:04.380
and then twist the line
four or five times over.

00:14:04.380 --> 00:14:07.590
Then you'll loop the end
into the top loop,

00:14:07.590 --> 00:14:10.510
which will create another loop,
and you'll pull the end through there.

00:14:10.510 --> 00:14:14.560
Once you slowly pull both ends
to close it off, you're done.

00:14:14.560 --> 00:14:17.440
This is called a clinch knot.

00:14:17.440 --> 00:14:19.060
That's so technical.

00:14:19.060 --> 00:14:21.480
Well? Do you think you've got it down?

00:14:21.480 --> 00:14:24.360
I definitely know you're
super talented, Hiyori!

00:14:24.360 --> 00:14:26.650
That's not what I was asking...

00:14:26.650 --> 00:14:30.490
This twisty part is super hard...

00:14:32.740 --> 00:14:34.580
I did it!

00:14:36.500 --> 00:14:39.830
Huh? You're not getting ready?

00:14:39.830 --> 00:14:41.710
Koi's not going to be fishing.

00:14:41.710 --> 00:14:43.960
Huh? Why though?

00:14:43.960 --> 00:14:48.170
I don't want to get burnt,
and it's cheaper to just buy the fish.

00:14:48.170 --> 00:14:52.010
I can't believe I heard that from
someone who works at a fishing shop!

00:14:53.100 --> 00:14:57.140
But I'm glad I got to
come here again with you, Koi.

00:14:57.140 --> 00:14:59.940
R-Really?

00:15:01.230 --> 00:15:05.730
Girls! I'm gonna get a head start!

00:15:05.730 --> 00:15:10.860
Anyway, I'll be watching
over my dad today.

00:15:10.860 --> 00:15:12.530
Okay, let's give it a try.

00:15:12.530 --> 00:15:16.200
Okay, uh...

00:15:16.200 --> 00:15:18.870
First, confirm that
there's no on behind me!

00:15:18.870 --> 00:15:21.620
It is pretty dangerous if you
accidentally hit someone.

00:15:21.620 --> 00:15:26.500
Don't put too much strength into the
casting or wave the line too much...

00:15:29.010 --> 00:15:31.260
Your loop's a mess.

00:15:31.260 --> 00:15:34.050
Stop staring! You're making me nervous!

00:15:34.050 --> 00:15:35.930
Oh, sorry.

00:15:37.100 --> 00:15:39.770
Has she been practicing
how to cast at home?

00:15:39.770 --> 00:15:41.730
Sometimes in our yard.

00:15:41.730 --> 00:15:44.480
Well, I guess she did just start...

00:15:44.480 --> 00:15:47.360
It'll probably take her
a while to get the hang of it.

00:15:47.360 --> 00:15:49.740
I mean, I'm still not good at it either.

00:15:49.740 --> 00:15:51.860
Pretty sure you've got all the
other high-school girls beat, Yamahi.

00:15:51.860 --> 00:15:55.030
Hey, I did it!

00:15:55.030 --> 00:15:56.490
Why weren't you watching?!

00:15:56.490 --> 00:15:58.370
Oh, sorry...

00:15:58.370 --> 00:16:00.790
Out of all possible times...

00:16:00.790 --> 00:16:03.500
Well, what do you want us to do?

00:16:03.500 --> 00:16:05.840
I-Is something eating at it?

00:16:05.840 --> 00:16:08.250
U-Um, uh...

00:16:08.250 --> 00:16:11.760
Calm down. You don't need to
reel it in when you're fly fishing.

00:16:11.760 --> 00:16:13.510
Oh, right!

00:16:13.510 --> 00:16:16.640
I hold the line with my
right pointer finger and...

00:16:16.640 --> 00:16:19.390
Pull it in with my left hand!

00:16:22.690 --> 00:16:24.100
It got away...

00:16:24.100 --> 00:16:27.070
It's okay! Let's calm down
for the next one.

00:16:27.070 --> 00:16:29.230
You were also late on your hooking, too.

00:16:29.230 --> 00:16:30.440
Hooking?

00:16:30.440 --> 00:16:35.320
It's when you hook the fly into the fish's
mouth by pulling the rod or the line.

00:16:35.320 --> 00:16:39.450
Fish tend to spit out the bait
as soon as it realizes it's fake.

00:16:39.450 --> 00:16:41.750
You probably shouldn't get distracted.

00:16:41.750 --> 00:16:45.250
Okay! I won't look away next time!

00:16:51.970 --> 00:16:53.090
Huh?

00:16:53.090 --> 00:16:55.510
I think the fish can sense your malice.

00:16:55.510 --> 00:16:59.060
Woo! I got a one cast, one hit today!

00:17:01.560 --> 00:17:03.100
Hey, it's tugging.

00:17:04.560 --> 00:17:06.560
That's amazing, Hiyori!

00:17:08.310 --> 00:17:11.820
See that spot where
the water's pouring out?

00:17:11.820 --> 00:17:16.490
Fish love spots like that,
so try aiming over there.

00:17:16.490 --> 00:17:17.910
Okay!

00:17:20.040 --> 00:17:21.580
Wh-What?

00:17:21.580 --> 00:17:24.410
You're like an instructor, Yamahi.

00:17:24.410 --> 00:17:27.380
I-I'm not trying to be...

00:17:27.380 --> 00:17:29.670
You've grown up.

00:17:29.670 --> 00:17:34.470
When you were little, you were so shy that
you were constantly hiding behind me.

00:17:34.470 --> 00:17:36.300
Oh, stop.

00:17:37.260 --> 00:17:42.140
It's just that Koharu's... a bit unique.

00:17:42.140 --> 00:17:45.230
I feel like I need to keep my eye on her.

00:17:45.230 --> 00:17:50.070
She's a problem child, so
I don't really have time to be shy.

00:17:50.070 --> 00:17:54.780
And... she said she wanted
to get better at fly fishing.

00:17:57.950 --> 00:18:01.700
Hiyori! They're about
to release more fish!

00:18:01.700 --> 00:18:04.330
Got it! I'm gonna head over.

00:18:04.330 --> 00:18:05.580
Okay.

00:18:06.580 --> 00:18:11.540
Man, I'm not getting a single bite,
but casting is somehow really fun.

00:18:13.420 --> 00:18:14.590
Okay, doom and gloom?!

00:18:14.590 --> 00:18:17.630
Wh-What's wrong?
Did you want to fish after all?

00:18:17.630 --> 00:18:19.220
Want to borrow my fishing rod?

00:18:19.220 --> 00:18:21.010
No.

00:18:22.350 --> 00:18:23.770
Yeah...

00:18:23.770 --> 00:18:24.390
"Gloom"

00:18:23.770 --> 00:18:24.390
Yeah...

00:18:24.390 --> 00:18:26.730
"Gloom"

00:18:24.390 --> 00:18:26.730
I really don't.

00:18:26.730 --> 00:18:29.230
"Gloom"

00:18:26.730 --> 00:18:29.230
Now she's even gloomier...

00:18:29.230 --> 00:18:29.940
Now she's even gloomier...

00:18:29.940 --> 00:18:33.780
But you've come here
before with Hiyori, right?

00:18:34.730 --> 00:18:38.240
Every once in a while,
when we were little.

00:18:38.240 --> 00:18:41.570
Our families were friends.

00:18:41.570 --> 00:18:47.000
I stopped going fishing,
but we remained close.

00:18:47.000 --> 00:18:53.170
Yamahi would always cling to my back,
so I thought of her as my little sister.

00:18:53.170 --> 00:18:58.510
I always thought that
I had to take care of her.

00:18:58.510 --> 00:19:00.140
But...

00:19:00.140 --> 00:19:02.550
Miss Hiyori Yamakawa.

00:19:04.470 --> 00:19:07.640
Okay, quiet, everyone.

00:19:07.640 --> 00:19:12.480
What's wrong?
Did something happen at home?

00:19:12.480 --> 00:19:15.860
Yeah, something like that.

00:19:20.240 --> 00:19:23.780
Was there anything I could actually do?

00:19:23.780 --> 00:19:29.830
I'm sure any condolences
would've felt empty.

00:19:29.830 --> 00:19:35.250
The ocean... looked like an area
I wasn't allowed to step foot into.

00:19:37.760 --> 00:19:41.930
If only I could just barge in
without a care in the world like you.

00:19:41.930 --> 00:19:44.930
Yay... I think that was a compliment?

00:19:44.930 --> 00:19:46.890
It was.

00:19:48.390 --> 00:19:52.020
I... have no right to be her friend.

00:19:52.020 --> 00:19:55.110
Do you really need the right
to be someone's friend?

00:19:56.690 --> 00:19:58.740
Nah, you don't.

00:19:58.740 --> 00:20:03.160
I'm pretty sure if you can just smile
around each other, that's all you need.

00:20:08.410 --> 00:20:10.410
Maybe...

00:20:10.410 --> 00:20:14.380
I shouldn't have been so scared
and barged in myself.

00:20:14.380 --> 00:20:17.460
But Hiyori is my little sister!

00:20:17.460 --> 00:20:19.630
She's legally my little sister!

00:20:19.630 --> 00:20:21.550
Yeah, yeah.

00:20:21.550 --> 00:20:25.890
Yamahi would mention this in her messages
all the time, but you really are unique.

00:20:25.890 --> 00:20:27.850
D'oh!

00:20:27.850 --> 00:20:30.560
She somehow seems shocked
by this development.

00:20:30.560 --> 00:20:36.190
Hiyori doesn't message me at all.
Maybe I'm not her friend after all...

00:20:36.190 --> 00:20:39.070
Ah, so that's it.

00:20:39.070 --> 00:20:43.150
Hey, has anyone ever
told you you're a handful?

00:20:49.620 --> 00:20:53.460
Yeah... she really is unique.

00:20:55.330 --> 00:20:58.630
Wow, that was so much fun!

00:20:58.630 --> 00:20:59.630
Yes!

00:20:59.630 --> 00:21:01.590
"Not a single catch"

00:21:01.880 --> 00:21:04.590
Sorry I left you alone, Koharu.

00:21:04.590 --> 00:21:08.350
I haven't done this in a while
so I got a bit too excited.

00:21:08.350 --> 00:21:12.980
It's okay... As long
as you had fun, Hiyori.

00:21:12.980 --> 00:21:14.640
I'm sorry. Really.

00:21:14.640 --> 00:21:16.980
You can just go fishing again.

00:21:16.980 --> 00:21:19.110
I'll tag along, too.

00:21:20.940 --> 00:21:23.030
Really?!

00:21:23.030 --> 00:21:24.610
Yeah.

00:21:24.610 --> 00:21:26.070
You sure you aren't pushing yourself?

00:21:26.070 --> 00:21:28.200
Absolutely positive.

00:21:28.200 --> 00:21:32.950
I-I'm sorry for always
forcing my hobby onto you.

00:21:32.950 --> 00:21:36.210
Well, just come shopping
with me next time.

00:21:36.210 --> 00:21:37.960
Let's go buy some summer clothes.

00:21:37.960 --> 00:21:39.210
I wanna go, too!

00:21:39.210 --> 00:21:40.880
Really? That's it?

00:21:40.880 --> 00:21:46.010
Well, you spend all of your allowance
on fishing clothes and gear, don't you?

00:21:46.010 --> 00:21:47.760
Wait, I'm buying some, too?

00:21:47.760 --> 00:21:52.270
You're in high school now, so you
need to wear something cuter.

00:21:52.270 --> 00:21:53.520
Right, Koharu?

00:21:53.520 --> 00:21:57.650
Yup. I was just thinking those sneakers
were pretty lame, to be honest.

00:21:57.650 --> 00:21:59.110
That's so mean!

00:22:03.190 --> 00:22:05.950
Koharu's a nice girl.

00:22:05.950 --> 00:22:10.160
I was worried when I heard
Hiyori's mom was going to remarry, but...

00:22:10.160 --> 00:22:13.120
Wow, you can actually think about
something other than fishing.

00:22:13.120 --> 00:22:15.160
Don't say that with such a serious face.

00:22:15.160 --> 00:22:17.370
You're going to make
your dear ol' dad cry.

00:22:22.050 --> 00:22:24.840
I don't think there's
anything to worry about.

00:23:55.060 --> 00:23:56.890
"Next Time"

00:23:56.890 --> 00:23:59.520
"Next Time"
Question time. What's the
fly you float on the water?

00:23:59.520 --> 00:24:00.350
"Next Time"
Dry!

00:24:00.350 --> 00:24:03.270
"Next Time"
Correct. Then what about the
one you sink to the bottom?

00:24:03.270 --> 00:24:04.110
"Next Time"
Nymph!

00:24:04.110 --> 00:24:06.860
"Next Time"
Correct. Then how about the one
that looks like a small fish?

00:24:06.860 --> 00:24:06.980
"The correct answer: streamer"
Correct. Then how about the one
that looks like a small fish?

00:24:06.980 --> 00:24:07.940
"The correct answer: streamer"
Stalker!

00:24:07.940 --> 00:24:09.860
"The correct answer: streamer"
That, my dear, is a crime.
